WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.148
The best mental model is to treat the inner query as
a result producer The

00:00:06.175 --> 00:00:12.096
inner query produces something The outer query then
uses that result

00:00:13.927 --> 00:00:18.071
The result might be one value a set of values or
rows that behave like

00:00:18.085 --> 00:00:23.774
an intermediate table Before writing the SQL ask
what shape the outer

00:00:23.787 --> 00:00:29.373
query needs That question prevents many common
subquery errors
